I need a digital transformation strategy that goes beyond digitizing processes: it must articulate how the digital redefines the value proposition, operations, and business model, to unlock investment decisions, align the board of directors, and deliver an actionable roadmap. Produce: (1) starting point; (2) 'from–to' thesis that separates efficiency from reinvention; (3) three dimensions with diagnosis, target, and digital bet; (4) enabling capabilities with gap; (5) horizons with measurable outcomes; (6) impact vs. feasibility matrix and no-regret first moves; (7) metrics, risks with mitigation, and success conditions. If any essential datum is missing, ask me before executing.
