Method: (1) Triage separating a real leak (monotonic growth that does not drop after a full GC) from seasonal footprint, fragmentation, or a cache warming up; if there is no evidence, stop. (2) Capture of baseline after warmup plus two or more comparable snapshots under sustained load. (3) Differential comparison sorted by retained size, not shallow; the signal is the delta of instances and retained bytes. (4) Following dominators/GC roots down to the named anchor. (5) Isolation to a concrete pattern (growing collection, cache without limit, live listeners/callbacks, closures, unclosed resources, thread-locals, statics, natives). (6) Verification with a reproducible experiment. (7) Correction plus anti-regression guardrail.

Closure criterion: the diagnosis delivers type and location of the leak, retention chain down to a named GC root, actionable correction, and regression prevention. Mark [ASSUMPTION] every inference without direct evidence from the profile. If the runtime, version, tool, or profile data is missing, ask for it before proceeding; do not invent. Consider edge cases: off-heap/native leak (RSS vs heap), slow leak, false positive from a warming cache, multiple leaks (isolate the dominant one by bytes).

MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

