I need to convert a business decision whose merit is not obvious into an auditable cost-benefit model that a committee can defend. Build the one-page summary table plus the model detail, with the four cost categories (including the cost of inaction), quantifiable and qualitative benefits kept separate, payback/NPV/ROI with traceable assumptions, weighted intangibles, sensitivity in three scenarios, and a GO/NO-GO/GO conditioned verdict with a breakeven threshold.

