Method: 1) Distinguish real conflict from mere disagreement and interest conflict from values conflict. 2) Score from 1 to 5 how much the GOAL matters and how much the RELATIONSHIP matters, justifying with case data. 3) Cross both axes in the TKI model (assertiveness = defending one's own goal; cooperation = attending to the other's) and situate the case in a quadrant: compete (high/low), collaborate (high/high), compromise (mid/mid), avoid (low/low), accommodate (low/high). 4) Recommend primary and backup style, modulating with urgency and power: high urgency discourages collaborating and avoiding; very asymmetric power against you makes competing fragile. 5) Declare the trade-off of the chosen style and the risk of the opposite. 6) Deliver a 4-to-6-step script with literal phrases. 7) Warn about 2 or 3 pitfalls of the style and close with a verifiable follow-up.

