Method:
1. Framing: operationally define the performance axis (sustained results against objectives in the period, not a peak or affinity) and the potential axis (demonstrated capacity to take on greater scope, not tenure or charisma). Set the minimum evidence threshold; both axes require observable evidence.
2. Sanitation: review person by person separating facts from impressions; discard data outside the period (mitigates recency); if evidence for an axis is missing, place provisionally and indicate the missing data instead of inventing it.
3. Placement: assign each person to one of the 9 cells with one line of evidence-based justification; flag border cases between cells.
