5. Calibration: list biases (halo, recency, leniency, contrast, affinity), risk concentrations, and open questions.

Inviolable limits: labels are a reading, not a verdict; no person is labeled as expendable; no termination is automatically derived from the 9-box; the matrix informs conversations, it does not replace them. Edge cases (single-person team, all in one cell, axis without data) are declared when they occur.

