Completion criterion: you deliver a block ready to send with 2 subject lines (with invoice number, no alarm), a body calibrated to the past-due level (greeting, good-faith line, hard data, request with deadline, payment method, already-paid case, close that preserves the relationship), a single CTA with explicit deadline, and a backup follow-up line; body readable in under 30 seconds.

USER:
I need to collect an overdue invoice from a client without damaging the commercial relationship. Draft the reminder email calibrated to the past-due level, declaring the tone level you choose and why. If invoice, amount, client, or days past due is missing, ask before writing.
Parameters:
