A professional meeting just ended and I need to put the agreements in writing before the context cools off. Draft a ready-to-send post-meeting thank-you email: a subject line naming the topic and anticipating next steps, a brief thank-you, purpose and agreements in no more than three sentences, next steps in a scannable table (action + owner + date), a follow-up proposal if applicable, availability for questions, reference to attachments, close, and signature. If any critical data is missing or any action lacks an owner or date, ask me before inventing.

Data:
