I need an operational runbook to execute a recurring operation or recover from an incident step by step, that any shift team member can follow without depending on my memory or availability. Before drafting, restate what you are going to document and present your plan; if an essential datum is missing, ask for it instead of inventing.

Deliver a one-to-three page runbook with: (1) Header (name, purpose in one sentence, version, date, owner). (2) Trigger and scope, distinguishing recurring operation from incident and declaring what is inside and outside scope. (3) Responsible and escalation (role, shift, to whom and how to escalate). (4) Prerequisites (systems, accesses, permissions, prior validations, and point of no return if one exists). (5) Numbered step-by-step procedure: each atomic step with responsible, exact command or location, and an observable verification check as a gate; flag destructive steps. (6) Complete operation success verification. (7) Failure modes and recovery table (symptom, probable cause, recovery action) with rollback path to the last known safe state. (8) Time window and service limit that triggers escalation. (9) Close (verifiable criteria, remaining evidence, close communication). (10) Maintenance (owner, review cadence, update triggers).

