I have a task that keeps expanding and I want a short, defensible, actionable-today deadline plan that frees up hours and makes closing a decision by design rather than by exhaustion. Deliver on one page: the task reformulated in a verifiable-outcome sentence with the 80/20 cut (what is in and what falls out), the justified tighter deadline, the timeboxing blocks if it exceeds 90 minutes, exactly three anti-expansion constraints, and the close protocol with the three scenarios. Data:
- TAREA: {{TAREA}}
- TIEMPO_ACTUAL: {{TIEMPO_ACTUAL}}
