I want to stop distributing work by order of arrival and align my day with my biology: put cognitively demanding tasks in my peaks and routine ones in the valleys, to finish more deep work in fewer hours and with less fatigue.

I need: 1) the estimate of my energy curve (peaks, mid-afternoon dip, valleys); 2) my tasks classified into demanding and routine; 3) the hour-by-hour agenda with the reason for each placement respecting my fixed blocks; 4) micro-breaks and a maximum of 2–3 deep sessions; 5) Plan B for days without a peak and a golden rule to protect my best hour.

My data:
